<title>UK: NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil seen soft.</title>
<headline>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil seen soft.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE low sulphur straight-run fuel oil prices were notionally softer on Monday as crude oil futures slipped but talk was thin, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no talk at all,&quot; one regular seller said. He said $140 a tonne fob NWE was &quot;a reasonable ballpark price,&quot; following trade at this level last week.</p>
<p>Trade in Russian E-4 was thin and dealers said they saw the price at around $127 cif NWE.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
